-- title:
--   Expansion of power series along substituted generators
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring and let $n, d$ be natural numbers. Let $\rho : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to B[\![x_0,\dots,x_{n-1}]\!]$ be an $n$-tuple of multivariate formal power series in $n$ variables over $B$, each of whose constant coefficients vanishes, and let $b : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![x]\!]$ be a $d$-tuple of power series. Assume that the images of the $b_j$ in the quotient ring $B[\![x]\!]/I$, where $I$ is the ideal generated by the set of the $\rho_i$, span that quotient as a $B$-submodule, i.e. the $B$-span of the range of $j \mapsto \mathrm{Ideal.Quotient.mk}\,I\,(b_j)$ is the whole module. Then for every $f \in B[\![x]\!]$ there exists a $d$-tuple $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,d \to B[\![y_0,\dots,y_{n-1}]\!]$ of power series in $n$ variables such that
--   $$f = \sum_{j} \mathrm{subst}\,\rho\,(c_j)\cdot b_j,$$
--   where $\mathrm{subst}\,\rho\,(c_j)$ denotes the substitution of the $\rho_i$ for the variables of $c_j$ (legitimate since the $\rho_i$ have zero constant coefficient). No finiteness, local, noetherian or freeness hypothesis on $B$ is imposed, and the $c_j$ are not asserted to be unique.
--
--   This is the existence half of the statement that a $B$-module generating family for $B[\![x]\!]/(\rho)$ yields an expansion of every power series with coefficients substituted from $\rho$; it is the formal-geometry analogue of an adic successive-approximation argument. It is used in the treatment of formal modules and formal groups, for instance in establishing uniqueness of such expansions under additional freeness hypotheses and in comparing ideals generated by substituted series.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_exists_eq_sum_subst_mul_of_span_quotient_eq_top.lean

